; Terra Infinite - private credentials. COPY THIS FILE TO Config/Secrets.ini AND FILL IN YOUR OWN KEYS.
; Config/Secrets.ini is listed in .gitignore and must never be committed. UTerraSecretsSubsystem reads this file
; (or the environment variables named below) at start-up; the project runs without any key using open data.
;
; Precedence: environment variable > Config/Secrets.ini > empty (open-data fallback).

[Terra.Secrets]
; Cesium ion access token (https://ion.cesium.com/tokens). Environment variable: TERRA_CESIUM_ION_TOKEN
; Enables Cesium World Terrain (asset 1), Cesium OSM Buildings (asset 96188), Bing/Sentinel imagery and, if your ion
; account has it enabled, Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles (asset 2275207). Free tier for non-commercial use.
CesiumIonToken=

; Google Maps Platform API key with "Map Tiles API" enabled, for Photorealistic 3D Tiles streamed directly from
; https://tile.googleapis.com/v1/3dtiles/root.json. Environment variable: TERRA_GOOGLE_TILES_KEY
; LICENSING (read before enabling): Google's Map Tiles API terms require showing Google's attribution/logo whenever
; the tiles are visible, forbid caching tiles beyond the session, forbid using them offline, forbid removing or
; obscuring the attribution, and bill per root-tile request after the free monthly quota. Do not ship builds with a
; key baked in. When this is empty, Terra uses the open fallback stack (see docs/UNREAL.md):
;   Cesium World Terrain or open terrain (AWS Terrarium / Copernicus DEM) + OSM buildings (ODbL, attribution
;   "(c) OpenStreetMap contributors") + Natural Earth (public domain) + open railway/road/airport data (OSM/ourairports).
GoogleTilesKey=

; Optional: self-hosted 3D Tiles endpoint (e.g. a tileset built from open data). Environment: TERRA_TILESET_URL
TilesetUrl=
